{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>May Dan be, may</b> the tribe of <b>Dan be — a snake upon the way</b> to kill the nations, and his prowess will be extraordinary, like the prowess of a snake that kills with a slight thing, as we find with Samson: 'with the jawbone of a donkey I struck a thousand men.'" "<b>Shefifon.</b> From the root of 'הוא ישופך ראש' (he shall bruise your head). <b>And his rider falls backward</b> — behind the horse, and falls before Dan his pursuer."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:12.927768656Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}